# Regenerating test ELFs

These binaries are synthetic RISC-V ELFs (no GNU toolchain required).

```
python3 tests/lit/Inputs/gen_elfs.py
```

Equivalent hand-written sequences:

- `hello_rv32.elf` / `hello_rv64.elf` (addr `0x10094`):
  - `addi sp, sp, -16`
  - `sw ra, 12(sp)`
  - RV64 only: `addiw a0, a0, 0` then `ld a0, 0(sp)`
- `branches_rv64.elf`: `beq` / `bne` / `jal` / `jalr`
- `compressed_rv32.elf`: `c.li a0, 1` then `addi a0, a0, 1`

If a real `riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc` is available, an equivalent source would be:

```
riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -march=rv64i -mabi=lp64 -nostdlib -o hello_rv64.elf snippet.s
```
